<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Bhoi dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">1541 CE – 1560 CE (approx.) · capital Cuttack</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived dynasty that took the throne of Odisha after the Gajapatis, whose fall opened the region to the Karrani Afghans.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/govinda-vidyadhara">Govinda Vidyadhara</a>, a minister of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gajapati-kingdom">Gajapati Kingdom</a>, killed the last heirs of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prataparudra-deva">Prataparudra Deva</a> and seized the throne at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuttack">Cuttack</a> in 1541. His family, the Bhoi dynasty, inherited a kingdom already reduced by losses to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/golconda-sultanate">Golconda Sultanate</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Bhoi rulers continued the Gajapati title and the royal role in the cult of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jagannath">Jagannath</a> at Puri, but faced constant revolts by nobles and pressure from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/golconda-sultanate">Golconda Sultanate</a> and the Afghan rulers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a>. Their short reigns were dominated by palace intrigue.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 1559 to 1560 the minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mukunda-deva">Mukunda Deva</a> overthrew the last Bhoi rulers. He was defeated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karrani-dynasty">Karrani Afghans</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> in 1568, ending independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>. Bhoi descendants were later recognised as rajas of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-khurda">Kingdom of Khurda</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/bhoi-dynasty.jpg" alt="Bhoi dynasty" width="320" height="262"><figcaption>Image: Amshpatten · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khurda_kingdom_map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1541 CE – 1560 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Cuttack</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Govinda Vidyadhara</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism (Jagannath cult)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Odia</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bhois of Odisha</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1550&amp;focus=bhoi-dynasty" aria-label="Bhoi dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6993 1421 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Bhoi dynasty lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7313 1677L7310 1674"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7310 1674h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7313 1677h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7313 1677h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Cuttack. <a href="/atlas?year=1550&amp;focus=bhoi-dynasty">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
